    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1198-a3">

                <pb facs="0977" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg861"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">General Beltrán to the American Consul</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 273.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ejercito Nacional, Seccion de Operaciones
                                Mixtos</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tejeria</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Gen. Agustín Valdez has put in my
                    possession the communication in which you, as dean of the consular corps, have
                    requested an interview.</p>
                <pb facs="0978" n="862" xml:id="pg862"/>
                <p>As chief, which I am, of the forces which operate in this district, I inform you
                    that it will be a pleasure to have the interview take place.</p>
                <p>For the purpose, I request that you and the consuls and vice consuls who so
                    desire come to Tejería at 4 p.m.</p>
                <p>I will be at the entrance to the town at your orders.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joaquín Beltrán.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
